{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731748Z","id":"4643b8805198331cfd586ef4c720626da877005020b1d2d06bf4883a5b223513","body":{"detail":"channel_events(within) collects for the whole window; the negative checks (lines 387, 425, 476) pay it in full on purpose.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"143d09c57b3760bfb6f63632c6fd6fd946ce15eeeab169ff23e251a9db9078ca"},"summary":"The channel tests wait 3 to 5 s windows to show no second event arrives","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731776Z","id":"b42d4ebfa66df83f60c7952b63600300af453be578868ad719498bbe400d1897","body":{"detail":"With CLAX_TEST_BIN unset, clax_bin builds clax once per process, and under nextest each test is a process, so each build replaces target/debug/clax while other tests run it. The same fallback is in crates/clax-hooks/tests/golden.rs:13-37. just test and the gates set CLAX_TEST_BIN.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"2f5d33d51f0897726481ac38e2e851d02c82deab59fd8c48d6ffcaa7fe5ff839"},"suggested_fix":"A nextest setup script that sets CLAX_TEST_BIN, once that feature is stable.","summary":"A bare cargo nextest run races on target/debug/clax","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:06:13.534619Z","id":"4b2a4b22b89354139a88d2fc937ad057089716704044def190d0138e8d81ad75","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aac4e8e9","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs is gone; clax-mcp, clax-hooks, clax-server and clax-cli tests take clax from clax_fake_exe::clax_bin (crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs), which runs a stable-bin.sh copy kept by content, never target/debug/clax in place. Evidence: 'env -u CLAX_TEST_BIN cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-cli -p clax-fake-exe --no-fail-fast' -> 'Summary [77.790s] 552 tests run: 552 passed, 1 skipped'; 'env -u CLAX_TEST_BIN cargo test -p clax-mcp --test integration open_status' -> '1 passed'.","supersedes":"b42d4ebfa66df83f60c7952b63600300af453be578868ad719498bbe400d1897","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:01.003810Z","id":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","body":{"detail":"browser_thread (a multipart POST /api/artifacts/<raid>/threads with the public instance's cookie, Host and Origin) is here, in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs:36 and in crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:2220 (browser_thread_on); all three drive clax_testkit::remotes::Public. async fn agent(ts) -> ClaxTools (register a session, build DaemonClient and ClaxTools) is repeated in crates/clax-mcp/tests/connect_instance.rs:14, remote_artifacts.rs:19, publish_public.rs:71 and site_access.rs:12. clax-testkit may depend on clax-mcp (SERVER includes MCP in scripts/check-crate-layers.py).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"42441812f14c02ecff79a0b28553d0796e068b257d3d1b047487216d3f438d79"},"suggested_fix":"Add Public::browser_thread(raid, cookie, anchor, body) -> Value to crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs and delete the three copies; add one agent-tools helper (in clax-testkit, or a tests/common module in clax-mcp) for the ClaxTools setup.","summary":"The browser-thread test helper is now copied in three test files, and the ClaxTools agent setup in four","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:28:55.926999Z","id":"c82db36a1982179587e2d8b3e6085d5fddeced5847e4f92d7c1c7db41aa731c1","body":{"detail":"The same multipart POST with Public's cookie, Host and Origin is at crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs:48-70, crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs:34-56 and crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:2224-2244 (browser_thread_on); they differ only in anchor, cookie source and return value. agent(ts) is identical apart from the session name in crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs:19-28, connect_instance.rs:14-22, publish_public.rs:71-79 and site_access.rs:12-20. scripts/check-crate-layers.py:77 allows clax-testkit SERVER, which includes MCP (line 51), so the helper can live in clax-testkit.","kind":"comment","references":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","summary":"confirmed: browser_thread is copied in three test files and the ClaxTools agent setup in four","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:16:49.960451Z","id":"e724722f0edbf78696fdfadcf8c88635d3c0759a691757943cb30c3e9ca13864","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:43aa70f60","summary":"Public::browser_thread (crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs) and clax_testkit::mcp::agent_tools replace the three browser_thread copies (crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs, crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs, crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs browser_thread_on) and the four agent(ts) helpers (connect_instance.rs, remote_artifacts.rs, publish_public.rs, site_access.rs). bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-testkit:all: 11 of 11 pass.","supersedes":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T19:14:51.926286Z","id":"daa43a18b9b896d9529b04e77446597cc545d7af63d0bb85c6fba4ebf5f8948f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e724722f0edbf78696fdfadcf8c88635d3c0759a691757943cb30c3e9ca13864","summary":"Commit 43aa70f60 cited by this close was re-signed as bc3970641 (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T22:37:03.954623Z","id":"23c5bedaa6da2067fe91fc9c41516d05b909669243883f3b3c3343175f54d78d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs runs the heartbeat loop (tokio interval, Delay on a missed tick) and forward_notices (1 s pause after an empty answer at once, back-off 1 s to 30 s) inline in shim::run, in the spawned `clax mcp` these tests drive, so paused tokio time cannot reach them. heartbeats_advance_last_seen_at checks that last_seen_at advances; heartbeats_never_start_a_daemon_but_tool_calls_do waits for the shim's 'heartbeat failed' warning in shim.log. a_daemon_that_cannot_start_is_reported_as_unreachable no longer bounds the shim's exit at 3 s: it checks that the exit comes, under the hang guard, and that the shim logged no expiry of END_TIMEOUT ('ending the session timed out', 'reports still unsent'). Checking the periods needs the loops reachable in process with a clock, a change to product code.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":317},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"c6c25f136deea45b19e467b36d8110f05c35fb63a5bb1db9773139cd264a6e39"},"summary":"The shim's heartbeat period and its notices polls' pacing and back-off are not checked","tags":["testing","timing","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/comments.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T22:37:03.954693Z","id":"9fa4680cd6c86cb70beb342bd7779a3304abc01bf30c0acd4da92f12eda006da","body":{"detail":"assert_ran_out checked waited_s <= the caller's elapsed seconds, and the timeout_s: 0 case checked the caller waited at least 1 s by its own clock. Both read the wall clock in the test and are gone: the checks now rest on the daemon's waited_s >= the timeout. A waited_s inflated past the real wait, or a tool that reports a 1 s wait without making it, would pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":457},"content_hash":"00e5155443f9311db4eebdb7bfae6ad33b4600448e52bc3fce8cb3e3d428a8be"},"summary":"A ran-out wait's waited_s is no longer checked against the time the caller waited","tags":["testing","timing","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/open_status.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T22:37:03.954722Z","id":"7968164e8dfe553438012f20b4cc6351f7ac7873fad4fa70a113e0aae144df31","body":{"detail":"The hanging case measured the call: at least the 300 ms open wait, under 4 s. The opener now runs until the test's directory is gone, so an answer under the hang guard shows open does not wait for its exit; that it waited the open wait first is unchecked (it needs the test to read the wall clock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"7af167ca3606097c2579ed056c62b5d45ebef7fa619b35873f2b1fd2a0066016"},"summary":"Nothing checks that open waits its open wait before calling a running opener opened","tags":["testing","timing","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:57:18.098689Z","id":"6fcd32c440621e9abe9aa7c8bd3f9dd81ebcd59b908e4bf7e2e52d526a2b27c1","body":{"detail":"Before sending each comment the loop waits for `push.tier == \"notice\"` on GET /api/sessions/<sid>, under the comment \"Both poll: the session's push is the follower's\". The daemon reports that tier while `Followers::has(sid, FollowKind::Follower)` holds (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs:402 and 460), and `has` counts a follower whose last poll ended under `Followers::RECENT` (15 s) ago as well as one polling now (crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs:375-388). The first pass's `clax feedback follow --once` has just printed its line and exited when the second pass starts, so the second `until_get` returns on its first answer whatever the second follower is doing, and the comment is sent while that follower is most likely still starting. The pass still ends with one announcement (the channel leaves notices to a recent follower, crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:655, and the follower takes the notice on its first poll), so the test passes, but only the first pass has the channel and a follower both in a poll when the comment arrives. On origin/main the 500 ms sleep after each `c.follow(1)` gave both passes that state; the second pass is the one that shows the channel yields again after a follower has come and gone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":529},"end":{"line":535},"content_hash":"21114fb670d66a9769cee53daa19c417d46fa8d2299b3581b0ddb6fe8e8c4492"},"suggested_fix":"Wait on something only the new follower's poll makes true: for example a test-only route that counts the session's notices polls in progress by kind (as /api/_test/sessions/{id}/feedback/waiters counts feedback waits), asked until it shows one follower poll beside the channel's. Or state in the comment that the second pass sends its comment before its follower polls, and name what that pass is then checking.","summary":"In its second pass, a_comment_is_announced_once_across_channel_and_follow's wait for the follower is already true, so the comment is sent before the second follower polls","tags":["review","review:deterministic-tests-2026-11-12","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T19:01:06.708925Z","id":"90cce807c5f9ee1f2ef56ec7010364fe543d845eda8045e0e2f4b0bee4bc62a2","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs:529-535: each pass runs `c.follow(1)`, then `c.until_get(\"/api/sessions/{sid}\", |v| v[\"push\"][\"tier\"] == \"notice\")` under the comment \"Both poll: the session's push is the follower's\", then `send_comment`. `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs` shows this wait replaced `std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(500))` after `c.follow(1)`.\n\nWhat the wait reads: push_info answers `\"claude\" if live.follower => {\"tier\": \"notice\", …}` (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs:460) and `live.follower` is `followers.has(sid, FollowKind::Follower)` (sessions.rs:402). `Followers::has` (crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs:375-388) is `active.contains_key(&key) || last.get(&key).is_some_and(|t| t.elapsed() < recent)` with `recent` = `Followers::RECENT`, 15 s (feedback.rs:355), for a follower; `FollowGuard::drop` (feedback.rs:421-436) writes `last` whenever a notices poll ends. The route enters the guard for every notices poll (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:625).\n\nSo the first pass cannot reach `send_comment` until a follower poll has been counted, and that follower's poll has either ended (it printed and exited under `--once`, or was killed: `last` is written) or is still counted in `active`. The second pass begins at once after `follower.wait()` (channel.rs:559), well inside 15 s, so its `until_get` is true on its first GET whether or not the follower just spawned has made a request; the test thread's GET races a new process's start.\n\nThe pass still gets one announcement: the channel's poll takes nothing while `s.followers.is_following(&sid)` (routes/feedback.rs:655, 666-670), which is the same `has`, and the new follower takes the notice on its first poll. So the test passes, and the comment \"Both poll\" is true of the first pass only.\n\nThe kind is right: the wait that replaced the sleep does not wait for what its comment says in one of its two passes; nothing fails. The route the suggested fix models itself on exists (`/api/_test/sessions/{sid}/feedback/waiters`, used at channel.rs:578-581).","kind":"comment","references":"6fcd32c440621e9abe9aa7c8bd3f9dd81ebcd59b908e4bf7e2e52d526a2b27c1","summary":"confirmed: in the second pass the first pass's follower already makes push.tier \"notice\", so the wait returns on its first answer","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
